          "smoke/cabo-verde/mobile-open.png"
        ],
        "limitations": [
          "A higher or rear camera would be needed to evaluate the caldera opening directly.",
          "No continuous motion or fine hardware contact inspection performed."
        ],
        "mobile_observations": "Volcanic silhouette and brass clasp read clearly, but caldera basin/opening and symbolic cultivated details do not. Texture becomes muddy at this scale. Both states are fully framed.",
        "open_observations": "Stone underside, dark cavity, blue rim and rear hinges are visible. Dark interior limits floor/depth inspection. Terrain is concealed on opposite lid face. Projecting released latch remains within frame.",
        "promotional_finish_vs_geometry": "Concern is weaker runtime recognition of the named caldera and crater compared with promo. README describes a tested recess and opening; this review neither independently confirms nor contradicts those geometry measurements.",
        "terrain": "Volcanic cone and lower ridges carry through. Promo exposes a clearer crater opening and textured interior; default runtime angle emphasizes the peak, leaving crater depth and horseshoe caldera opening difficult to read, especially on mobile. This is a readability issue, not proof of a flat or missing crater.",
        "texture": "Mottled gray/brown stone with rust/ash bands persists. Promo is more granular and dimensional; runtime mottling can read cloudy concrete, while broad terrain color patches look applied/procedural. These align with disclosed stylization limitations.",
        "verdict": "needs-decision"
      },
